{"name":"Lizard","hex":"#7b6943","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lizard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A peninsula in southern Cornwall, England."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village in Landewednack parish, on the peninsula near Lizard Point, Cornwall, the most southerly village in England, also known as Lizard Town"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lizard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lizard","blocks":[{"text":"Lizard is the common name used for all squamate reptiles that are not snakes, encompassing over 7,000 species. They have a cosmopolitan distribution, ranging across all continents except Antarctica, as well as most oceanic island chains. Extant lizard species vary in size from the 13.5 mm (0.53 in) nano-chameleon and the 14–18 mm (0.55–0.71 in) Jaragua dwarf gecko to the 3-meter-long Komodo dragon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Hemidactylus_platyurus_%28Flat-tailed_House_Gecko%29_on_white_background%2C_focus_stacking.jpg/330px-Hemidactylus_platyurus_%28Flat-tailed_House_Gecko%29_on_white_background%2C_focus_stacking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizard","wikidata":"Q15879"},{"title":"Lizard (character)","blocks":[{"text":"The Lizard is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by Stan Lee and Steve Ditko, he first appeared in The Amazing Spider-Man #6 as an enemy of the superhero Spider-Man. While the character has retained this role throughout most of his subsequent appearances, he has also been portrayed as a tragic antihero and occasional ally of Spider-Man. Connors is sometimes an ally of Spider-Man just as himself, and not necessarily as his alter ego."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/Lizard_%28Curt_Connors%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"htt